{"type":"text","timestamp":1794528706395,"sessionID":"ses_e2dc43e05ffeeCgmmPyuO8zh4b","part":{"id":"prt_1d23ef1000028aWvqf9VXj8dGv","sessionID":"ses_e2dc43e05ffeeCgmmPyuO8zh4b","messageID":"msg_1d23edae30019MoFms0k4MGO4c","type":"text","text":"T035 complete.\n\n## Files written\n\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/scratch/relabel-ids.mjs` — walks only JSON string values in the four named files, replaces the four old ids at token boundaries, and records file, row id and field. It never emits prompt text: its only stdout is the count line.\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/scratch/relabel-list.txt` — 5 rows:\n\n```\nholdout-prompts.jsonl P0-CMD-002 skill_top_1\ngate2-golden-prompts.jsonl golden-speckit-plan-changelog expectedSkillAny[0]\nskill-advisor-regression-cases.jsonl P0-CMD-002 expected_top_any[0]\nlocal-native-approved-divergences.json rr-iter3-070 localTop\nlocal-native-approved-divergences.json rr-iter3-070 reason\n```\n\nThe fifth row is the old id embedded in the divergence entry's `reason` sentence. The verify condition (no old-id match anywhere in the four files) requires it, and it was the only way to reach the required 5 changes.\n\nEdited data files (each changed only by the id tokens):\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/holdout-prompts.jsonl`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/fixtures/gate2-golden-prompts.jsonl`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/fixtures/skill-advisor-regression-cases.jsonl`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/parity/fixtures/local-native-approved-divergences.json`\n\n## Verify output\n\n```\n$ node .../scratch/relabel-ids.mjs\nrelabeled 5 values in 4 files\n$ rg -c \"command-spec-kit-(plan|complete|implement|resume)\\b\" <four files>\nrg exit=1\n$ wc -l < .../scratch/relabel-list.txt\n       5\n```\n\nNo match output (exit 1) means the pattern prints nothing. Additional checks: `node --check` on the script exits 0, all four files still parse, and a HEAD-vs-working comparison confirms each file differs only by the four id token replacements.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Checkbox in `tasks.md` left unticked as instructed.\n- No other files touched, no git state changed. Pre-existing untracked `scratch/briefs/` and `scratch/logs/` were not mine and were left alone.\n- `plan.md` was not read because the task line does not point at it.","time":{"start":1794528702720,"end":1794528706395}}}
